      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are giving up on using Linux\u0027s checkpatch.pl for verifying printf %p. We had no %p extensions before, so this check did nothing in the past. Now because %pT doesn\u0027t exist in Linux, checkpatch.pl complains.\n\nMy goal is to turn on the format checking in the compiler, The compiler punts on %p for the most part, other than to validate that you do in fact pass a pointer. But given that we don\u0027t make any effort to match Linux\u0027s behavior for %p extensions, using checkpatch.pl to validate %p doesn\u0027t make sense either way.",
